{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites re-measured on origin/main 403719c01ce (base 083620b0 was 333+ commits behind and predates the `[0.14.0]` release of 2026-10-30).\n\n`gen_env_registry.render()` (`scripts/gen_env_registry.py:400`) unions derived names only for `REBAR_MCP_*` (`MCP_ENV_VARS`, `:406-409`), so most settable `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` names never reach `docs/env-vars.md`. **Do not hardcode the counts.** At sweep time `_SECTIONS` x `_canonical_env_name` yielded 105 canonical names against 109 documented rows, 68 missing; those figures move as siblings `cb2b` and `b939` land ahead of this story (`b939` *removes* two names). Re-derive before implementing; let the test compute them.\n\nThe canary keeps a \"one-release\" rollback source (`scripts/canary_bridge.py:140-143,687`; `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml:28,34,54,134`) two releases after ADR 0094.\n\n**CHANGELOG — the premise changed.** `git merge-base --is-ancestor` shows both commits this story files shipped in **v0.14.0**, and in neither v0.13.0 nor v0.13.1: `334ee94` \"Remove scheduled public deprecations\" and `81da792` \"Retire the HLC rollback switch\" (both 2026-09-03). They do **not** belong in `[Unreleased]` — that was right only before `[0.14.0]` was cut. `334ee94`'s two bullets are misfiled under `[0.13.0]` (`:258-503`) at `:489-496` (the `force=`/`force_close` normalization) and `:498-502` (the `openai-chat` fallback); both move to `[0.14.0]` `### Changed` (`:13`, subsection `:15`). `81da792` has no entry and needs one under `[0.14.0]`. `[Unreleased]` (`:11`) is empty — only *this epic's* unreleased work goes there.\n\n## Approach\n- **Registry (decision: derive all).** In `render()` replace the `MCP_ENV_VARS`-only union (`:406-409`) with a loop over `_SECTIONS` calling `_canonical_env_name(sect, key)`, attributing each to `src/rebar/_config_sections.py (canonical env name of {sect}.{key})`; keep the `MCP_ENV_VARS` union for `REBAR_MCP_DEDUP` (in `MCP_ENV_VARS`, not a config key). `_canonical_env_name` is at `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:289`; `_SECTIONS` is importable from `rebar._config_schema` (precedent: `scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py:48`). Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`. Do **not** change `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:63-81` — dozens of new `env_var::` entries would trip `check_mechanism_delta --check` with no marker path; update its docstring `:8-15` and `docs/architecture.md:629` to state the deliberate asymmetry: the ratchet censuses definition sites, and a derived name's site is its `_SECTIONS` row, already counted as `config_key`/`feature_flag`. Tests: `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` add `test_every_canonical_env_name_is_documented` — derive the set from `_SECTIONS`, assert each appears as a ``| `NAME` |`` row, assert **no literal count**. `:43-56` unchanged (`REBAR_PUSH` still absent). `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py` needs no edit (`_llm_*` helpers only).\n- **Canary.** `scripts/canary_bridge.py`: delete `:140-143` and `:687`; `cmd_check_heartbeat` calls `_check_status_heartbeat` directly; keep `_check_github_heartbeat` for the `NEVER_RUN` bootstrap (`:203-212`, ADR 0094 `:81-82` forbids dropping it), make `bootstrap` a required keyword and drop the `if bootstrap` conditional at `:345`. Workflow: delete the `status_source` dispatch input (`:28` description, `:34` choice) and the `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` job env (`:54`); `:134` becomes `python scripts/canary_bridge.py check-heartbeat`. The named `run:` steps censused as `ci_gate::` rows in `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:299-310` stay; `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE` has no `env_var::` row, so the mechanism ratchet is unaffected. Docs: `docs/jira-sync-setup.md:191` (delete sentence), `:294` (delete row); `docs/adr/0094-reconciler-last-pass-two-witness-status.md` append a dated \"Status\" paragraph after `:82`.\n- **Canary tests — the file set AC2's grep compels.** `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py:71` remove the key and have `hb_env`'s runner answer `rebar bridge status` with `{\"verdict\":\"NEVER_RUN\"}` so the run-history math is exercised via bootstrap. `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py`: `:74`, **`:122`**, `:145`, and delete the rollback test covering `:168`. `:122` sets the key to `\"status\"`, not `\"github-api\"`, which is why earlier passes missed it — AC2's grep does not care, and leaving it keeps AC2 non-empty. `tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py:133` remove the key.\n- **CHANGELOG.** Move `:489-496` and `:498-502` out of `[0.13.0]` into `[0.14.0]` `### Changed`. Add under `[0.14.0]`: \"- **BREAKING (pre-1.0): the `REBAR_HLC=0` rollback switch is removed.** The HLC is always on; the variable is ignored (commit `81da792`, ticket `fdd1-12fa-ce83-45d1`).\" Leave `:620` (historical cross-reference) and `:1342` (the 2025 entry recording `force_close`'s introduction) where they are. Under `[Unreleased]` (`:11`) create the needed subsection and add only this epic's unreleased work: the alias-tombstone entry, the `[llm]` unknown-key entry, the test-hooks entry (\"test-only `REBAR_HLC_NOW` / `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` are no longer read by rebar\"), and \"`docs/env-vars.md` now lists every `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` override\". Mirror in `docs/release-notes.md`.\n\n## Scope\n`scripts/gen_env_registry.py`, `scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py` (docstring only), `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/architecture.md:629`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `scripts/canary_bridge.py`, `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`, `docs/adr/0094-reconciler-last-pass-two-witness-status.md`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`. Out of scope: `detect_config.py:63-81` detector logic, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py`, the `_check_github_heartbeat` bootstrap path (ADR 0094 `:81-82`), and the historical `docs/release-notes.md:696-698` and `CHANGELOG.md:620,1342`.\n\n## Testing\n- `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` clean after regeneration; spot-check `grep -n 'REBAR_VERIFY_REQUIRE_PLAN_REVIEW_FOR_CLAIM\\|REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS' docs/env-vars.md` both present. Do not assert a row total.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge*.py tests/scripts/test_canary_status_refs_heldout.py tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q`.\n- Edge: `canary_bridge.py check-heartbeat --source github-api` -> argparse error (exit 2); `REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE=github-api` with a `NEVER_RUN` fake -> bootstrap witness, output contains `(last-pass producer bootstrap fallback)`.\n- `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1 Every name produced by `_SECTIONS` x `_canonical_env_name` appears as a row in `docs/env-vars.md`, asserted by the new `test_every_canonical_env_name_is_documented` deriving both sides; `gen_env_registry.py --check` clean. No literal count appears in the AC, the test, or Testing — upstream siblings move every figure.\n- [ ] AC2 `git grep -n 'REBAR_CANARY_HEARTBEAT_SOURCE\\|github-api' -- scripts .github tests` is **empty**; `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` green. Pre-state to confirm before implementing: **14 hits** across 5 files, all in scope (the grep does not over-match). `test_canary_bridge_heldout.py:122` is one of them. (BRE alternation is deliberate: `git grep -E` ignores `\\b`, so an `-E` rewrite can match nothing and pass vacuously.)\n- [ ] AC3 `CHANGELOG.md` `[0.13.0]` no longer contains the `force=`/`force_close` or `openai-chat` bullets; `[0.14.0]` carries both plus a `REBAR_HLC` entry; `[Unreleased]` carries this epic's four entries. Verified by asserting each bullet's section membership, not a line-number threshold — `:620` and `:1342` are historical and must not move.\n- [ ] AC4 `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports `new=0`; `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793424494266492506,"uuid":"ab52f564-8c7c-4807-80cc-97d6791b3876"}